/-!
# Bounded-generated quasi-coherent submodules exhaust a quasi-coherent module

Source: Stacks Project, Properties, Tag 077N, lemma-colimit-kappa
(blueprint: lem-sfb-qcoh-bounded-submodule-union).

Subobjects encode actual subsheaves modulo the unique isomorphism commuting with
inclusion. The diagram and cocone below use Mathlib's canonical subobject arrows.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- The inclusion-ordered set of all quasi-coherent `κ`-generated subsheaves of `F`.
Source: Stacks Tag 077N, last paragraph of `lemma-colimit-kappa`.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-qcoh-bounded-submodule-union). -/
noncomputable abbrev BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (κ : Cardinal.{u}) :=
  {N : Subobject F // SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent (N : X.Modules) ∧
    IsCardinalGenerated (N : X.Modules) κ}

/-- The actual inclusion diagram of the bounded-generated quasi-coherent subsheaves.
Source: Stacks Tag 077N, last paragraph of `lemma-colimit-kappa`.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-qcoh-bounded-submodule-union). -/
noncomputable def boundedQuasiCoherentSubmoduleDiagram {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (κ : Cardinal.{u}) : BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ ⥤ X.Modules :=
  (OrderHom.toFunctor
    { toFun := fun N : BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ ↦ N.val
      monotone' := fun _ _ h ↦ h }) ⋙ Subobject.underlying

/-- The cocone consisting of the subsheaf inclusions into `F`.
Source: Stacks Tag 077N, last paragraph of `lemma-colimit-kappa`.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-qcoh-bounded-submodule-union). -/
noncomputable def boundedQuasiCoherentSubmoduleCocone {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (κ : Cardinal.{u}) : Cocone (boundedQuasiCoherentSubmoduleDiagram F κ) where
  pt := F
  ι :=
    { app := fun N ↦ N.val.arrow
      naturality := fun _ _ f ↦ Subobject.underlying_arrow
        ((OrderHom.toFunctor
          { toFun := fun N : BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ ↦ N.val
            monotone' := fun _ _ h ↦ h }).map f) }

/-- There is an infinite cardinal depending only on `X` such that every quasi-coherent
module is the colimit of the inclusion-ordered small, nonempty, directed set of all its
quasi-coherent submodules locally generated by at most that cardinal many sections.
No quasi-compactness, quasi-separatedness or Noetherian condition is imposed.

Source: Stacks Tag 077N, `lemma-colimit-kappa`, with Tag 077L for local generation
(blueprint: lem-sfb-qcoh-bounded-submodule-union).

Proof:
1. Choose an affine cover and affine covers of all pairwise intersections, symmetrically.
   By `lem-weil-pbc-affine-opens-basis` and `lem-coef-small-family-regular-bound`, fix
   an infinite cardinal bounding all these index sets, independently of the module.
2. On the cover and its overlaps use `lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-affine-sections`,
   `def-pc-module-pullback` and `lem-weil-pbc-module-restriction-open-immersion-colimits`
   to identify restriction with tensoring. By `def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product`,
   choose finite supports expressing each restricted generator from the other chart.
3. Starting with any bounded family of seeds, adjoin all these supports repeatedly.
   `lem-sfb-infinite-cardinal-square` bounds the size at every stage by the same cardinal.
4. Take the countable union. The same cardinal arithmetic preserves the bound and the
   two generated spans on each overlap agree by symmetry and closure under supports.
5. Using `lem-weil-pbc-affine-tilde-gamma-adjunction` and
   `lem-weil-pbc-spec-module-tilde-sections`, associate modules to these spans; take their
   images inside the given module by `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-cokernel-image`.
6. Naturality of the affine counit identifies their sections on each affine overlap.
   Restriction preserves quasi-coherence; the counit identifies the subsheaves, and the
   sheaf condition extends equality to each whole intersection.
7. By `lem-weil-pbc-glue-sheaves-of-modules`, glue their inclusions. The actual range
   consists of sections lying in all the local subsheaves; it is quasi-coherent by
   `pqf-def-coherent`, cardinal-generated, and contains all chosen seeds.
8. Actual subsheaves inject into the product of the powersets of the section sets over
   all opens (`def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category`, `def-weil-size-convention`). Hence
   this poset is small. The zero subsheaf belongs, even on the empty scheme.
9. The image of the sum of two members contains both and belongs: use
   `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-direct-sum`, the cokernel-image lemma, and the
   cardinal bound on the union of two generating families. Thus the poset is directed.
10. The singleton-seed construction exhausts sections on every chosen affine. By
    `lem-pc-scheme-modules-grothendieck-abelian` the small colimit exists, and
    `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-colimit-affine-sections` computes its sections.
    Its canonical map to the given module is surjective by exhaustion and injective
    because a representative already embeds into the given module.
11. The affine counit identifies this map with an isomorphism on each affine. Its
    inverses agree on intersections by uniqueness and glue by the gluing lemma.
    Transporting the colimit cocone along this isomorphism gives exactly the cocone
    of inclusions (`def-weil-pbc-category-colimit`).
-/
theorem exists_cardinal_boundedQuasiCoherentSubmodule_colimit (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    ∃ κ : Cardinal.{u}, Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ ∧
      ∀ F : X.Modules, SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent (R := X.ringCatSheaf) F →
        Small.{u} (BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ) ∧
        Nonempty (BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ) ∧
        Directed (· ≤ ·) (fun N : BoundedQuasiCoherentSubmodules F κ ↦ N) ∧
        Nonempty (IsColimit (boundedQuasiCoherentSubmoduleCocone F κ)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
